<?php

/**
 * @file
 * SO-ARM API module.
 *
 * Exposes the `robot_knowledge` content type (defined by soarm_core) for
 * read and write access through Drupal core's JSON:API module, so that
 * external clients (ROS2 nodes, the LeRobot upload scripts, browser
 * front-ends, etc.) can list, create, update and delete knowledge posts
 * without a custom REST controller.
 *
 * Endpoints (all under the site base URL, e.g. http://localhost:8080):
 *
 * - GET  /jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge
 *     List/filter knowledge posts. Anonymous users can read published
 *     posts (the `access content` permission, already granted to the
 *     anonymous role by the standard install profile, is sufficient).
 *     Example: filter by title
 *       curl -H "Accept: application/vnd.api+json" \
 *         "http://localhost:8080/jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge?filter[title]=Dishwasher"
 *
 * - GET  /jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge/{uuid}
 *     Read a single post.
 *
 * - POST /jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge
 *     Create a post. Requires a user with the `create robot_knowledge
 *     content` permission (granted to the `soarm_contributor` role by
 *     soarm_core) authenticated with HTTP Basic auth (provided by core's
 *     basic_auth module), and a `Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json`
 *     body describing the node's attributes/relationships.
 *       curl -u contributor:password \
 *         -H "Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json" \
 *         -H "Accept: application/vnd.api+json" \
 *         -d '{"data":{"type":"node--robot_knowledge",' \
 *            '"attributes":{"title":"...","field_outcome":"success"},' \
 *            '"relationships":{...}}}' \
 *         http://localhost:8080/jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge
 *
 * - PATCH/DELETE /jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge/{uuid}
 *     Update or delete a post the user owns (or has permission to edit).
 *
 * - POST /jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge/{field}
 *     Upload a binary file (video, calibration data, trajectory data,
 *     camera images, ...) to one of the node's file fields ahead of
 *     creating/updating the node itself. The response's `data.id` is the
 *     file UUID to reference from a `relationships.{field}` block on a
 *     subsequent node create/update request.
 *       curl -u contributor:password \
 *         -H "Content-Type: application/octet-stream" \
 *         -H 'Content-Disposition: file; filename="episode_001.mp4"' \
 *         --data-binary @episode_001.mp4 \
 *         http://localhost:8080/jsonapi/node/robot_knowledge/field_video
 *
 * `hook_install()` in soarm_api.install flips core's
 * `jsonapi.settings:read_only` flag to FALSE (that config is owned by the
 * jsonapi module, so soarm_api must not ship its own copy of it under
 * config/install; adjusting it in hook_install() is the accepted pattern).
 *
 * EXTENSION POINT (WebSocket/SSE): a real-time "new post" push channel for
 * dashboards or ROS2 subscribers would hook into
 * hook_ENTITY_TYPE_insert() for `node` (bundle `robot_knowledge`) — right
 * after JSON:API commits the new node, that hook would serialize the node
 * and publish it to a Mercure hub or an SSE endpoint (e.g. via an injected
 * HTTP client service), so subscribers receive the post without polling
 * the collection endpoint. No such hook is implemented yet.
 */

declare(strict_types=1);
